 no writes, `void` return; asserted against pre-poisoned buffers plus canaries either side | `row59_60_gjk_cache_no_op` | [x] |"," ","-Rows 14, 15, 16, 18, 19 and 24 are undefined behaviour in the C (uninitialised","-reads, out-of-bounds reads, NULL derefs). For these the C has no","-reproducible observable behaviour, so a byte-equality assertion is","-meaningless. They are covered as follows instead:","+## Generic FFI boundaries (beyond the table)"," ","-* row 17 asserts the *well-defined* half of row 16 (that `c2MakeProxy` writes","-  nothing for an out-of-range enum) using a caller-owned, pre-poisoned buffer;","-* rows 18/19/24 (NULL derefs) are not called in-process, since a `SIGSEGV`","-  would take the test harness down with it;","-* rows 14/15 are exercised only to confirm neither library aborts.","+`tests/phase_c_errors.rs::generic_boundaries` additionally sweeps, for both","+libraries at once:","+","+* every `C2_TYPE` value `0..=8` through `c2MakeProxy` (valid *and* out of range);","+* `c2Support` with `count` = `0`, `1`, `8` (the proxy array size) and `9`","+  (one past it);","+* simplex `count` = `-1, 0, 1, 2, 3, 4, 5` — one step past every documented","+  case — through `c2L`, `c2D`, `c2GJKSimplexMetric`, `c2Witness`, `c22`, `c23`;","+* `c2GJK` with `use_radius` = `-1, 0, 1, 2, INT_MIN, INT_MAX`;","+* `c2GJK` with `cache->count` = `-1, 0, 1, 2, 3`.","+","+`abi_layout_matches_c` pins every struct size (`c2v` 8, `c2r` 8, `c2x` 16,","+`c2Circle` 12, `c2AABB` 16, `c2Capsule` 20, `c2GJKCache` 36, `c2Proxy` 72,","+`c2sv` 36, `c2Simplex` 152) and `sizeof(int) == sizeof(unsigned) == 4`, so the","+\"same error value\" assertions above really are comparing the same bytes.","+","+## UB rows — what is asserted instead","+","+Rows 13, 14, 15, 16, 18, 19 and 24 are **undefined behaviour in the C**:","+uninitialised reads, out-of-bounds reads/writes, or NULL dereferences. A","+bit-equality assertion is meaningless for them because the C has no","+reproducible result — this was *measured*, not assumed:","+","+* rows 14/15: **11 882** of the sampled out-of-range-index configurations gave","+  different answers between the two libraries, and the C returned *different","+  values for the same input on different runs* (e.g. `1106020886` then","+  `1102845220`), because it reads uninitialised `c2Proxy::verts` slots;","+* row 16: calling `c2GJK` with an out-of-range enum **reliably SIGSEGVs** the C,","+  since the uninitialised `pA.count` reaches `c2Support` unchecked;","+* row 13: `verts[4]` overruns `c2Simplex` by 28 bytes and smashes `c2GJK`'s own","+  stack locals.","+","+They are therefore covered as follows:","+","+* **row 17 asserts the well-defined half of row 16** exhaustively — that","+  `c2MakeProxy` writes *nothing* for an out-of-range enum — using","+  caller-owned, pre-poisoned proxies and ~2000 random out-of-range `u32`","+  values. That is the entire enum behaviour the C actually defines.","+* **rows 14/15 are executed** for both libraries (`run_both_no_assert`) to","+  confirm neither aborts, and the divergence count is reported.","+* **rows 13, 18, 19, 24 are deliberately not executed in-process**: they would","+  either SIGSEGV the harness or corrupt its stack. Each has a test that pins","+  down the structural premise it rests on (struct sizes for row 13; the absence","+  of any count/NULL guard in `c2Support` for row 24).","+* Phase B keeps the *defined* paths clean by folding carried-over cache indices","+  back into range (`clamp_cache`), so rows 54/56 of `CONFIGS.md` test the","+  documented behaviour rather than accidental UB."]}],"originalFile":"# ERRORS.md — Phase C error-surface table\n\nDerived mechanically from `c_src/src/lib.c`. Grep results:\n\n```sh\ngrep -n 'assert\\|RETURN_ERROR\\|return -1\\|return NULL\\|errno' src/lib.c   # -> 0 hits\ngrep -n 'if (!\\|<= 0\\|> 0\\|== 0'                              src/lib.c   # -> 14 hits (listed below)\n```\n\n**There is no error enum, no `assert`, and no error return code anywhere in\nthe library.** Every public function either returns a value unconditionally\nor returns `void`. The \"rejection surface\" therefore consists of:\n\n* **defensive null checks** that silently substitute a fallback instead of\n  failing (`c2GJK`'s six pointer checks),\n* **`switch` / `default:` fall-throughs** that swallow out-of-domain\n  `count` and out-of-domain `C2_TYPE` enum values,\n* **unguarded divisions and square roots** whose sentinel is `inf` / `NaN`\n  rather than an error code,\n* **unvalidated indices / counts** read straight out of caller memory.\n\nEach row below is one distinct such branch. \"Expected C result\" is the exact\nobservable behaviour of the C, which the Rust must reproduce bit-for-bit.\n\n| #  | function | trigger (exact invalid input / condition) | expected C result |\n|----|----------|--------------------------------------------|-------------------|\n| 1  | `c2GJK` | `ax_ptr == NULL` | no deref; `ax = c2xIdentity()` = `{p:(0,0), r:{c:1,s:0}}`; runs normally |\n| 2  | `c2GJK` | `bx_ptr == NULL` | no deref; `bx = c2xIdentity()`; runs normally |\n| 3  | `c2GJK` | `outA == NULL` | `*outA` not written; return value + other outs unaffected |\n| 4  | `c2GJK` | `outB == NULL` | `*outB` not written; return value + other outs unaffected |\n| 5  | `c2GJK` | `iterations == NULL` | `*iterations` not written; return value unaffected |\n| 6  | `c2GJK` | `cache == NULL` | cache neither read nor written; simplex seeded fresh (`count=1`, `div=1`) |\n| 7  | `c2GJK` | `cache != NULL` but `cache->count == 0` | `cache_was_good == 0` → skips the read block → fresh seed; cache *is* written on exit |\n| 8  | `c2GJK` | `cache->count != 0` and `!(min<max*2 && metric < -1e8)` — i.e. essentially always | quirk: `cache_was_read = 1`, the stale simplex is trusted verbatim (no re-seed) |\n| 9  | `c2GJK` | `cache->count != 0` and `min_metric < max_metric*2 && metric < -1.0e8f` (needs a metric ≤ −1e8) | `cache_was_read` stays 0 → simplex re-seeded from vertex 0 |\n| 10 | `c2GJK` | warm cache with `cache->count == 3` (valid indices) | cache read, `s.count==3` on entry → first loop iteration hits `if (s.count==3)` → `hit=1`, `iter==0`, `dist==0`, `a==b` |\n| 11 | `c2GJK` | `cache->count < 0` (e.g. `-1`, `-1000`) | copy loop body never runs; `s.count` = the negative value; `c2GJKSimplexMetric` `default:`→0; `switch(s.count)` matches nothing; `count != 3`; `c2L` `default:`→(0,0); `c2D` `default:`→(0,0) → `dot(d,d)=0 < eps²` → break; `c2Witness` `default:` → `a=b=(0,0)`; `dist=0`; cache written back with the negative count (write loop skipped) |\n| 12 | `c2GJK` | `cache->count == 4` | reads `cache->iA[3]` / `cache->iB[3]`, which by struct layout alias `cache->iB[0]` and `cache->div`; writes `verts[3]` (= `s.d`, still in bounds). Fully deterministic, must match |\n| 13 | `c2GJK` | `cache->count > 4` (e.g. 5, 6) | out-of-bounds read past `iB[3]` and out-of-bounds write past `s.d` into `s.div`/`s.count`. Deterministic for a given layout; compared as-is |\n| 14 | `c2GJK` | `cache->iA[i]` / `cache->iB[i]` ≥ proxy `count` but < 8 (e.g. index 3 on a `C2_TYPE_CIRCLE` proxy whose `count==1`) | index is inside `c2Proxy::verts[8]` so no OOB, but the slot was never initialised by `c2MakeProxy` → **indeterminate in C** (reads uninitialised stack). Documented, not asserted |\n| 15 | `c2GJK` | `cache->iA[i]` ≥ 8 (e.g. 100) | genuine out-of-bounds read past `c2Proxy::verts` — UB, indeterminate. Documented, not asserted |\n| 16 | `c2GJK` | `typeA` or `typeB` is an out-of-range enum value (`3`, `7`, `255`, `(C2_TYPE)-1`) | `c2MakeProxy`'s `switch` has **no `default:`** → the `c2Proxy` local is left entirely uninitialised → `radius`/`count`/`verts` are indeterminate stack garbage. **UB in C**; documented, not asserted. (The well-defined half — that `c2MakeProxy` writes *nothing* — is asserted in row 17.) |\n| 17 | `c2MakeProxy` | `type` not in `{0,1,2}` (`3`, `4`, `255`, `0xFFFFFFFF`) | `switch` falls through with no `default:` → **not a single byte of `*p` is written**; a caller-prefilled `c2Proxy` buffer is returned bit-identical |\n| 18 | `c2MakeProxy` | `shape == NULL` with a valid `type` | dereferences NULL → `SIGSEGV`. Both libs crash identically; not exercised in-process |\n| 19 | `c2BBVerts` | `out == NULL` or `bb == NULL` | NULL deref → `SIGSEGV`; not exercised in-process |\n| 20 | `c2Support` | `count <= 0` (`0`, `-1`, `INT_MIN`) | `verts[0]` is read *before* the loop guard, then `for (i=1; i<count)` never runs → returns `0` |\n| 21 | `c2Support` | `count == 1` | loop never runs → returns `0` regardless of `d` |\n| 22 | `c2Support` | all dots equal, or `d == (0,0)` (every dot `0`, never `> dmax`) | returns `0` (first index wins ties) |\n| 23 | `c2Support` | some `verts[i]` component is `NaN` | `dot > dmax` is false for NaN → NaN candidates never win; `dmax` can be NaN from `verts[0]`, after which *no* later index wins → returns `0` |\n| 24 | `c2Support` | `verts == NULL` | NULL deref → `SIGSEGV`; not exercised in-process |\n| 25 | `c2Witness` | `s->count` not in `{1,2,3}` (`0`, `4`, `-1`) | `default:` → `*a = (0,0)`, `*b = (0,0)` |\n| 26 | `c2Witness` | `s->div == 0` (with `count` 1..3) | `den = 1.0f/0 = +inf`; for `count==1` the outputs are unaffected; for `count` 2/3 outputs are `±inf` or `NaN` (`inf * 0.0f`) |\n| 27 | `c2Witness` | `s->div` is `NaN` or `-0.0` | `den` is `NaN` / `-inf`; propagates into the weighted sums |\n| 28 | `c2L` | `s->count` not in `{1,2}` (`3`, `0`, `4`, `-1`) | `default:` → returns `(0,0)` |\n| 29 | `c2L` | `s->div == 0`, `count` 2 | `den = +inf` → components `±inf` / `NaN` |\n| 30 | `c2D` | `s->count` == `3` or any value outside `{1,2}` | `default:` → returns `(0,0)` |\n| 31 | `c2D` | `count == 2` and `a.p == b.p` (degenerate edge) | `ab = (0,0)`, `det2 = 0` which is *not* `> 0` → takes `c2CCW90((0,0))` → `(0,0)` |\n| 32 | `c2GJKSimplexMetric` | `s->count` not in `{2,3}` (`1`, `0`, `4`, `-1`) | `default:` shares the `case 1:` body → returns `0` |\n| 33 | `c2GJKSimplexMetric` | `count == 2` with equal points | `c2Len((0,0)) = sqrtf(0) = 0` |\n| 34 | `c2Norm` | `a == (0,0)` | `c2Len = 0`; `c2Div(a, 0)` → `1.0f/0 = +inf`; `0 * inf` → `NaN` in both components |\n| 35 | `c2Norm` | `a` has a `NaN` or `inf` component | `c2Len` → `NaN`/`inf`; result `NaN` components |\n| 36 | `c2Div` | `b == 0` | `1.0f/0 = +inf` → components `±inf`, or `NaN` when the component is `0` |\n| 37 | `c2Div` | `b == -0.0` | `1.0f/-0.0 = -inf` → sign-flipped `inf` / `NaN` |\n| 38 | `c2Div` | `b == NaN` | both components `NaN` |\n| 39 | `c2Len` | `a` huge (e.g. `1e38`) | `c2Dot` overflows to `+inf`; `sqrtf(+inf) = +inf` |\n| 40 | `c2Len` | `a` has a `NaN` component | `sqrtf(NaN) = NaN` (no domain error, sign of NaN preserved by `sqrtss`) |\n| 41 | `c2Maxv` | either operand has a `NaN` component | `(a.x) > (b.x)` is false whenever a `NaN` is involved → **`b`'s component is returned**, not `a`'s. Non-commutative NaN ordering must be reproduced |\n| 42 | `c2Minv` | either operand has a `NaN` component | `(a.x) < (b.x)` is false → **`b`'s component is returned** |\n| 43 | `c2Maxv`/`c2Minv` | `+0.0` vs `-0.0` | neither `>` nor `<` holds → `b`'s component is returned, so the *sign of zero* depends on argument order |\n| 44 | `c2Clampv` | `lo > hi` (inverted range, no validation) | no rejection: `c2Maxv(lo, c2Minv(a, hi))` → `lo` wins, result is `lo` |\n| 45 | `c2Clampv` | `a`, `lo` or `hi` contains `NaN` | NaN ordering of rows 41/42 composes; result follows the exact `b`-wins rule |\n| 46 | `c22` | `a.p == b.p` (degenerate, `u == v == 0`) | `v <= 0` is true → collapses to `count = 1`, `a.u = 1`, `div = 1` |\n| 47 | `c22` | `a.p`/`b.p` contain `NaN` (`u`, `v` both `NaN`) | `v <= 0` false, `u <= 0` false → `else` branch: `div = NaN`, `count = 2` |\n| 48 | `c23` | all three points equal (every `u`/`v`/`area` is `0`) | `vAB <= 0 && uCA <= 0` true → `count = 1`, `div = 1` |\n| 49 | `c23` | collinear points (`area == 0` → `uABC == vABC == wABC == 0`) | some `<= 0` guard fires; if it reaches the `else`, `div = 0` and `count = 3` (a `div == 0` simplex, feeding row 26) |\n| 50 | `c23` | points contain `NaN` (all comparisons false) | falls through every branch to the `else` → `div = NaN`, `count = 3` |\n| 51 | `c2GJK` | 20-iteration cap reached | `while (iter < 20)` exits with `iter == 20`; `*iterations = 20` |\n| 52 | `c2GJK` | `use_radius != 0` and `dist <= rA + rB` (overlap), or `dist <= FLT_EPSILON` | else-branch: `a = b = 0.5f*(a+b)`, `dist = 0` |\n| 53 | `c2GJK` | `use_radius != 0`, shrink makes the points coincide (`a.x==b.x && a.y==b.y`) | `dist` forced to `0` after the subtraction |\n| 54 | `c2GJK` | `use_radius != 0` and `rA + rB` overflows / is `NaN` (radius `1e38` or `NaN`) | `dist > rA+rB` false for NaN → midpoint branch, `dist = 0` |\n| 55 | `c2GJK` | `use_radius` is a value other than 0/1 (e.g. `2`, `-1`, `INT_MIN`) | C tests truthiness → any non-zero behaves exactly like `1` |\n| 56 | `c2GJK` | degenerate AABB with `min > max` (inverted box) | no validation; `c2BBVerts` produces a reversed winding → negative `area`, sign-flipped `c2Det2` results; still returns a finite `dist` |\n| 57 | `c2GJK` | degenerate capsule with `a == b`, or zero radius, or negative radius | no validation; negative radius makes `rA + rB` negative so the `dist > rA+rB` branch is taken and `dist` *grows* |\n| 58 | `c2GJK` | all shape floats are `NaN`/`inf` | NaN propagates; the loop exits via the `dot(d,d) < eps²` test being false and the `dup` test, or via the iteration cap; result is `NaN`/`0` |\n| 59 | `gjk_cache` | `reverse == 0` vs `reverse != 0` (`1`, `-1`, `0x80`, `'A'`) | selects which shape is A vs B in the final `c2GJK`; `char` truthiness only |\n| 60 | `gjk_cache` | `a9` / `b9` are `NULL`, or any float argument is `NaN`/`inf` | **`a9` and `b9` are never dereferenced by the C** → no crash, no writes, `void` return; the function is observably a no-op |\n\n## Notes on the UB rows\n\nRows 14, 15, 16, 18, 19 and 24 are undefined behaviour in the C (uninitialised\nreads, out-of-bounds reads, NULL derefs). For these the C has no\nreproducible observable behaviour, so a byte-equality assertion is\nmeaningless. They are covered as follows instead:\n\n* row 17 asserts the *well-defined* half of row 16 (that `c2MakeProxy` writes\n  nothing for an out-of-range enum) using a caller-owned, pre-poisoned buffer;\n* rows 18/19/24 (NULL derefs) are not called in-process, since a `SIGSEGV`\n  would take the test harness down with it;\n* rows 14/15 are exercised only to confirm neither library aborts.\n","userModified":false}}
