{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_bdrk_wmsebpaordw7zwkxjcihvyiknpnn2fv63nslll5uvnfx3nd4o7dq","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Verification complete. All four phases pass.\n\n## Bugs found and fixed in the Rust translation\n\nAll divergences were **real**, found by bit-exact differential testing against the C `.so`:\n\n1. **SSE `src1` NaN-payload selection (6 functions).** The C is built at `-O0`, so every float expression becomes a literal `ADDSS`/`MULSS`/`SUBSS`/`DIVSS`. Those instructions are asymmetric: when *both* operands are NaN, the surviving payload is whichever operand gcc put in the destination register. gcc's allocator does **not** consistently pick the left-hand source — e.g. `c2Add` emits `addss %xmm1,%xmm0` with `%xmm0 = b.x`, so `a.x + b.x` propagates **b**'s payload. LLVM freely commutes `fadd`/`fmul`, so plain `a + b` in Rust gave no control. Fixed by deriving the exact `src1` at every arithmetic site from `objdump` of the C `.so` and pinning it with `addss`/`subss`/`mulss`/`divss`/`fneg` helpers (each site carries the matching instruction as a comment). Affected `c2Add`, `c2Dot`, `c2Det2`, `c2Mulrv`, `c2MulrvT`, `c2L`, `c2Witness`, plus `c2Div`/`c2Mulvs`/`c2Sub`/`c22`/`c23`/`c2GJK`. This also removed a fragile `read_volatile` hack that only patched one symptom.\n\n## What the C does that can't be matched (measured, not assumed)\n\n`c2GJK` reading a cache whose vertex index exceeds the new proxy's `count` reads **uninitialised stack**: the C returned *different values for the same input on different runs* (`1106020886` → `1102845220`). Calling `c2GJK` with an out-of-range `C2_TYPE` **reliably SIGSEGVs** the C, because the uninitialised `pA.count` reaches `c2Support` unchecked. `ERRORS.md` marks these 7 rows `[UB]` and documents exactly what is asserted instead — notably row 17, which exhaustively proves the well-defined half (`c2MakeProxy` writes *zero bytes* for any of ~2000 out-of-range enum values).\n\n## Artifacts\n\n- `SYMBOLS.md` — 31/31 symbols, **0 missing, 0 extra**, no undefined non-libc symbols.\n- `ERRORS.md` — 60 rows: **53 with passing differential tests, 7 `[UB]`**.\n- `CONFIGS.md` — 71 rows, all passing under randomized inputs (fixed seed).\n- `run_all.sh` — builds the C, then loops every feature combo × profile, diffing symbols and running the suite.\n\n**88 tests pass in both `debug` and `release`** from a clean tree. Several rows assert branch coverage (`c23` must reach result counts 1/2/3, `c2D` both skew and CCW90 paths, etc.) so they can't pass vacuously, and `harness_loads_two_distinct_libraries` proves the suite isn't comparing one library against itself.\n\nTwo caveats worth flagging: `gjk_cache` (the only function in `lib.h`) never dereferences its `a9`/`b9` out-params and returns `void`, so it is observably a **no-op** — its verification rests on the `c2GJK` rows that cover its internal calls. And `ERRORS.md` row 51's 20-iteration cap is unreachable through the public API: over ~162 000 configurations the maximum observed was **4**."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1475,"cache_read_input_tokens":286431,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":1475,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"6c917cb3-3512-41c1-87cf-ea90c6ebff2f","uuid":"e9574040-e9f0-4478-a742-ac731fe62f5d","timestamp":"2026-09-05T08:30:11.692Z"}
