xmm0` with `%xmm0 = b.x`, so `a.x + b.x` propagates **b**'s payload. LLVM freely commutes `fadd`/`fmul`, so plain `a + b` in Rust gave no control. Fixed by deriving the exact `src1` at every arithmetic site from `objdump` of the C `.so` and pinning it with `addss`/`subss`/`mulss`/`divss`/`fneg` helpers (each site carries the matching instruction as a comment). Affected `c2Add`, `c2Dot`, `c2Det2`, `c2Mulrv`, `c2MulrvT`, `c2L`, `c2Witness`, plus `c2Div`/`c2Mulvs`/`c2Sub`/`c22`/`c23`/`c2GJK`. This also removed a fragile `read_volatile` hack that only patched one symptom.\n\n## What the C does that can't be matched (measured, not assumed)\n\n`c2GJK` reading a cache whose vertex index exceeds the new proxy's `count` reads **uninitialised stack**: the C returned *different values for the same input on different runs* (`1106020886` → `1102845220`). Calling `c2GJK` with an out-of-range `C2_TYPE` **reliably SIGSEGVs** the C, because the uninitialised `pA.count` reaches `c2Support` unchecked. `ERRORS.md` marks these 7 rows `[UB]` and documents exactly what is asserted instead — notably row 17, which exhaustively proves the well-defined half (`c2MakeProxy` writes *zero bytes* for any of ~2000 out-of-range enum values).\n\n## Artifacts\n\n- `SYMBOLS.md` — 31/31 symbols, **0 missing, 0 extra**, no undefined non-libc symbols.\n- `ERRORS.md` — 60 rows: **53 with passing differential tests, 7 `[UB]`**.\n- `CONFIGS.md` — 71 rows, all passing under randomized inputs (fixed seed).\n- `run_all.sh` — builds the C, then loops every feature combo × profile, diffing symbols and running the suite.\n\n**88 tests pass in both `debug` and `release`** from a clean tree. Several rows assert branch coverage (`c23` must reach result counts 1/2/3, `c2D` both skew and CCW90 paths, etc.) so they can't pass vacuously, and `harness_loads_two_distinct_libraries` proves the suite isn't comparing one library against itself.\n\nTwo caveats worth flagging: `gjk_cache` (the only function in `lib.h`) never de